{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1557030-anyone-here-just-for-a-cod-game","id":1557030,"title":"Anyone Here Just For a CoD game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-26T20:00:56-08:00","id":1557030,"title":"Anyone Here Just For a CoD game?","content":"Is there anyone here, that, was draw to CoD or NWoD based on reading the core-book(s) and not for the major splats (vamps, werewolves etc.)?<br /> <br /> Was anyone at a local gaming shop, back in the day, and picked up a NWoD hard-copy, read it, and said, &quot;This is the game for me&quot;?<br /> <br /> With only getting the core-rules just so they can play a vamp/mage/wolf etc.?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-27T04:17:29-08:00","id":1557042,"title":"","content":"I think 2E made some mechanical improvements. But the introductory material in the front of NWoD is incredible at setting the mood. I ran a straight CoD mortals game last year and it was great. And I'd do it again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-27T09:29:16-08:00","id":1557045,"title":"","content":"I was initially drawn to Mage, but continued to delve into the broader setting as my interest grew. While I did not buy it in the physical store, I love having a physical, hardcover copy whenever I can, it's just something special to me that digital can't capture, and the core books of CofD are amongst them.<br /> <br /> The core books like <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> and <i>Hurt Locker</i> are amongst my favorites. The design, the mechanics, the plot hooks and setting do an incredible job to get you excited to play a mortal, presenting tons of flavorful options and ideas. It's a very easy recommendation, as a incredible reference for rules and feel, a great resource to easing players into the setting and a great source of ideas for homebrew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-28T04:37:44-08:00","id":1557057,"title":"","content":"The first and still most successful game I personally run in CofD was pure blue-book mortals. Yes, I do find it great.<br /> <br /> While you can get it from the splat rule books, I think the best way to &quot;get&quot; the setting is through Core. Even if you plan only on running a splat, reading the core will help you a lot to acclimate yourself with the style and the reason behind design decisions.<br /> <br /> Above all, this is a mystery setting. Not horror, even, although inclined to it, but mystery. And every splat works by adding a layer on top of the mystery instead of replacing it. You don't have all the answers. You don't know how the world works. You'll face the weird, the absurd and the incomprehensible even way after you thought you were beyond this.<br /> <br /> By the way, that first game was all about mild supernatural crimes that looked like splat doings but weren't, yet had some real supernatural bite, as the alchemist that used human blood drained through two needle perforations in the neck, leaving a trail of &quot;vampire victims&quot;, but his concoctions were the real deal nonetheless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-02T18:31:01-08:00","id":1557218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1557030-anyone-here-just-for-a-cod-game?p=1557045#post1557045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was initially drawn to Mage, but continued to delve into the broader setting as my interest grew. While I did not buy it in the physical store, I love having a physical, hardcover copy whenever I can, it's just something special to me that digital can't capture, and the core books of CofD are amongst them.. . ..</div> </div> </div> </div>Years ago, I found Mage: the Awakening at a used bookstore for almost the asking price, new; I thought it was too expensive and, I'm really into Mage: the Ascension and I couldn't justify the cost: I regret not buying it when I could have. <br /> <br /> Back then, and kinda now, I was into Immortals, Second-Sight and Book of Spirits. Those, with the core-book, were all I really needed. I picked up Requiem and Foresaken later. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-02T18:34:16-08:00","id":1557219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1557030-anyone-here-just-for-a-cod-game?p=1557042#post1557042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think 2E made some mechanical improvements. But the introductory material in the front of NWoD is incredible at setting the mood. I ran a straight CoD mortals game last year and it was great. And I'd do it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>My favorite game to run and play one, in Old World of Darkness, are Mortals. I used the Vampire: the Masquerade Player's Guide's Mortal character-sheets; I loved it when I got my hands on Hunder's Hunted and finally had more numia for the mortals. I also ran just a Mortals: Dark Ages game, for like, a bit, were, the player's vampire-characters were, mortals in the past: I LOVE it. I do like straight up CoD games without any supers in them. But, they're always there, on the side-line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-03T03:58:04-08:00","id":1557226,"title":"","content":"It also has a lot of genre flexibility to it. Anything from like True Detective to Tales from the Loop. I ran a Space Marine game with CoD once. I know its pretty easy to port nWoD books over (Mysterious Places, Midnight Roads, etc.) but I wish Onyx Path would keep doing CoD books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T12:50:30-08:00","id":1557319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1557030-anyone-here-just-for-a-cod-game?p=1557042#post1557042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think 2E made some mechanical improvements. But the introductory material in the front of NWoD is incredible at setting the mood. I ran a straight CoD mortals game last year and it was great. And I'd do it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I like a lot of the 2E rules changes, I feel like the early 1E days had peak presentation. The then-nWoD core book is legitimately one of my top five core books of all time, and VTR 1E dripped crimson style. MTA 1E was also fantastic, and so was WTF, though I feel like the core book there struggled more than the other two. However, where it really came into its own were the sourcebooks: HG: The Rockies, Predators, Blood of the Wolf, etc. Total swag. <br /> <br /> Ghost Stories. Antagonists. Precinct 13. Damnation City. The Chicago book. Everything just hit with so much style and occupied a niche that really felt fresh, exciting, full of possibilities. Not to mention like every single one of the main expansions for CTL 1E. <br /> <br /> I love the newer stuff, but those days sure brought us a ton of really great books. That nWoD core just had so much style and inspired so many story ideas just on its own. I still sometimes do things with just that flavor, and I have a desire to revisit an old PBP that would be pure mortals in a ghost story. Purely on the strength of those original offerings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T20:24:11-08:00","id":1557438,"title":"","content":"My group played through one of the tales from Ghost Stories as vanilla mortals. It was a lot of fun, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29019-darkondreams","name":"DarkonDreams","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}